-- statement:
--   **The copy `0 → rZ`** as a two-array step (`g A _ = (A, A)`).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegAxCopy`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.AxC.copyAx_ok {dA : Fin HS} (hA : DAok dA) (P : Prm) (n : ℕ) (src : ℕ → ℕ) (D k B w : ℕ)
--       (hk : k ≤ D) (hB : DescB P n src D k B) (hw : w ≤ B) :
--       Ax.Pass2OK Isym tbl (copyRS dA).code dA (descAx6 P n src D k)
--         (fun A Bl => Bl = [] ∧ A.length = (List.ofFn (tD6 P n D)).prod ∧ GB w A)
--         (fun A _ => (A, A)) (cCopy (2 * (List.ofFn (tD6 P n D)).prod) B)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The axis program: the copy `0 → rZ` (after pass 2) and the swap `0 ↔ rZ` (before pass 7)
--
--   Both read the count `2·pre·t·post` (the number of integers of an axis array) off the axis
--   descriptor `descAx6 = [k, pre, post, s, t, …]` on `dA` (restored), on the scratch stacks `1 … 7`.
--
--   * `cntRS dA`: pushes `2·(pre·(t·post))` on `CN = 5` (`sp_cnt`);
--   * `copyAx dA`: `gflat L ++ l` on `0` and `l₂` on `rZ` ↦ `gflat L ++ l₂` on `rZ`, stack `0`
--     unchanged (`copyAx_runs`);
--   * `swapAx dA`: `gflat A ++ l` on `0`, `gflat B ++ l₂` on `rZ` ↦ `gflat B ++ l` on `0`,
--     `gflat A ++ l₂` on `rZ` (`swapAx_runs`).
--
--   Convention (`FineBody6`): every stack other than `0, dA, rZ` empty; `dA ∉ {0, …, 7, 53}`,
--   `dA < 56`.
